00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:44.640
single most important rule is what

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:46.560
researchers called the challenge skill

00:02:44.640 --> 00:02:48.480
balance. Whatever you're doing needs to

00:02:46.560 --> 00:02:51.200
be about 4% harder than what you

00:02:48.480 --> 00:02:52.921
currently can do comfortably. So just 4%

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:54.560
slightly above your current level. If

00:02:52.921 --> 00:02:55.920
[music] the task is too easy, your

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:58.000
brain's going to check out. You get

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:59.760
bored. If the task is too difficult, you

00:02:58.000 --> 00:03:01.920
get anxious and overwhelmed. Eventually

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:04.239
you're going to procrastinate. So flow

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:06.480
is a state of mind just like your

00:03:04.239 --> 00:03:08.959
emotions. In order to get into this

00:03:06.480 --> 00:03:11.200
flow, you have to ride [music] that wave

00:03:08.959 --> 00:03:13.200
of emotional management. And if you see

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:15.040
in this chart, there is a clear channel

00:03:13.200 --> 00:03:16.560
that takes you there. But if you veer

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:18.720
off too far from the path, you're going

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:21.120
to lose your flow. So flow state lives

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:23.040
right between boredom and anxiety. This

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:25.120
is why video games are literally

00:03:23.040 --> 00:03:27.440
designed to [music] keep you in this

00:03:25.120 --> 00:03:29.200
zone. The difficulty skills with your

00:03:27.440 --> 00:03:31.040
skill level so you never get bored and

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:32.720
you never get overwhelmed. That's why

00:03:31.040 --> 00:03:34.319
