At this stage, time bends, your inner

00:09:24.880 --> 00:09:29.600
critic goes away, and this is the state

00:09:26.800 --> 00:09:31.440
to be in. Now, stage four is recovery. A

00:09:29.600 --> 00:09:33.440
lot of driven people do burn out at this

00:09:31.440 --> 00:09:35.680
stage because they skip the recovery.

00:09:33.440 --> 00:09:37.279
Unfortunately, a side effect of flow is

00:09:35.680 --> 00:09:38.880
that it depletes your neurochemistry. So

00:09:37.279 --> 00:09:40.720
after a deep flow session, your brain

00:09:38.880 --> 00:09:43.040
actually needs the rest. [music] It

00:09:40.720 --> 00:09:45.120
needs good food, water, and sleep. If

00:09:43.040 --> 00:09:46.880
you try to chase another flow block

00:09:45.120 --> 00:09:49.279
immediately, you might actually crash

00:09:46.880 --> 00:09:51.839
out. Your brain literally does not have

00:09:49.279 --> 00:09:53.839
enough chemicals available to go back in

00:09:51.839 --> 00:09:55.920
for round two. So give yourself a bit of

00:09:53.839 --> 00:09:57.519
permission to rest after a deep work

00:09:55.920 --> 00:09:59.200
session. Some of you guys may think that

00:09:57.519 --> 00:10:00.720
I travel a lot and I go on holidays all

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:02.800
the time or whatever, but because I

00:10:00.720 --> 00:10:04.880
determine my schedule these days, I

00:10:02.800 --> 00:10:07.040
literally do not take weekends off

00:10:04.880 --> 00:10:09.440
because I'm usually so locked in. And

00:10:07.040 --> 00:10:12.080
instead, what I do is I get a ton of

00:10:09.440 --> 00:10:14.079
work done ahead of time and then go away

00:10:12.080 --> 00:10:15.760
about once a month. That's my time to

00:10:14.079 --> 00:10:17.680
rest. Do what works for you, of course,

00:10:15.760 --> 00:10:20.000
but this works for me because I know how

00:10:17.680 --> 00:10:22.640
I work. So, the cycle looks like

00:10:20.000 --> 00:10:24.720
struggle, release, flow, recovery. Once

00:10:22.640 --> 00:10:26.240
you understand what comes next, you stop

00:10:24.720 --> 00:10:28.160
beating yourself up for the struggle

00:10:26.240 --> 00:10:30.320
part because you already know that's

00:10:28.160 --> 00:10:32.079
only step one. So, what might actually

00:10:30.320 --> 00:10:33.440
be blocking your flow? Because you could

00:10:32.079 --> 00:10:35.279
do everything right and still never

00:10:33.440 --> 00:10:37.040
access flow state if these things are

00:10:35.279 --> 00:10:39.040
present in your environment. Number one

00:10:37.040 --> 00:10:40.880
is your phone. I'm so serious. Research

00:10:39.040 --> 00:10:42.720
shows it takes 10 to 15 minutes of

00:10:40.880 --> 00:10:45.200
uninterrupted focus before you can even

00:10:42.720 --> 00:10:47.519
begin to enter a flow state. Deeper flow

00:10:45.200 --> 00:10:49.760
takes another 15 to 20 minutes. So,

00:10:47.519 --> 00:10:52.160
you're looking at 25 to 30 minutes

00:10:49.760 --> 00:10:54.079
minimum before you are fully in the

00:10:52.160 --> 00:10:55.680
zone. If you're trying to get into that

00:10:54.079 --> 00:10:57.760
state and then you go entertain yourself

00:10:55.680 --> 00:10:59.760
on your phone for a bit, boom, instead

00:10:57.760 --> 00:11:01.760
of locked in, you're locked out. You

00:10:59.760 --> 00:11:03.279
might have to start completely over. So,

00:11:01.760 --> 00:11:04.640
if you're checking your phone every 5

00:11:03.279 --> 00:11:06.720
minutes, you are actually making it

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:07.839
neurologically impossible to reach flow.

00:11:06.720 --> 00:11:10.000
Now, some of you guys might be like,

00:11:07.839 --> 00:11:11.839
"But I work on my phone." Well, me too.

00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:13.600
In that case, it's more about shutting

00:11:11.839 --> 00:11:15.839
off the apps that distract you.

00:11:13.600 --> 00:11:17.600
Sometimes what I even do is I put my

00:11:15.839 --> 00:11:19.440
phone on an airplane mode if I can help

00:11:17.600 --> 00:11:21.920
it and I pretend that I don't know what

00:11:19.440 --> 00:11:23.279
Instagram is. Like who is she even? I

00:11:21.920 --> 00:11:25.760
don't know her. Number two,

00:11:23.279 --> 00:11:27.440
multitasking. Your brain cannot

00:11:25.760 --> 00:11:29.040
multitask. I know some of you guys may

00:11:27.440 --> 00:11:30.720
think that you are multitasking pro, but

00:11:29.040 --> 00:11:32.800
I hate to break it to you, you are not.

00:11:30.720 --> 00:11:34.800
I had to learn this the hard way and

00:11:32.800 --> 00:11:36.640
it's okay. If you do unfocused things,

00:11:34.800 --> 00:11:38.720
you'll get unfocused results. What it

00:11:36.640 --> 00:11:40.720
actually does when you multitask is when

00:11:38.720 --> 00:11:42.399
you're rapidly switching between tasks

00:11:40.720 --> 00:11:45.040
because you can only do one thing at a

00:11:42.399 --> 00:11:47.760
time, each switch costes you something

00:11:45.040 --> 00:11:49.760
in your brain, your cognitive resources.

00:11:47.760 --> 00:11:51.680
It drains the exact neurochemicals that

00:11:49.760 --> 00:11:53.040
you need to maintain your flow state

00:11:51.680 --> 00:11:55.360
because you're going within this

00:11:53.040 --> 00:11:57.519
channel. The second you veer out, it's

00:11:55.360 --> 00:12:00.160
over. So if you're bouncing between your

00:11:57.519 --> 00:12:01.760
email, your projects, Slack messages,

00:12:00.160 --> 00:12:03.760
Google Docs, you are burning through

00:12:01.760 --> 00:12:06.240
dopamine and neuropen friend without

00:12:03.760 --> 00:12:08.320
ever getting the actual payoff. So

00:12:06.240 --> 00:12:10.320
instead of task switching, try task

00:12:08.320 --> 00:12:12.480
batching. Group similar task together

00:12:10.320 --> 00:12:14.240
and do them all in one block. I also

00:12:12.480 --> 00:12:16.240
like to take a mini break between each

00:12:14.240 --> 00:12:18.079
task about 2 minutes or 5 minutes so

00:12:16.240 --> 00:12:20.160
that I can rebuild my capacity. What

00:12:18.079 --> 00:12:22.160
that looks like is I would usually get

00:12:20.160 --> 00:12:23.920
up, get some water, you know, walk

00:12:22.160 --> 00:12:27.120
around a little bit, about two minutes,

00:12:23.920 --> 00:12:29.519
I go back. Rest, guys, is mandatory.

00:12:27.120 --> 00:12:31.040
Number three, vague goals. If you sit

00:12:29.519 --> 00:12:32.959
down, your goal is to just simply work

00:12:31.040 --> 00:12:36.000
on my business, your brain has nothing

00:12:32.959 --> 00:12:37.760
to lock onto. Flow requires clear,

00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:39.600
specific, actionable, and achievable

00:12:37.760 --> 00:12:41.760
goals. So, not just work on my business.

00:12:39.600 --> 00:12:43.519
Instead, you're I don't know exporting

00:12:41.760 --> 00:12:45.200
Excel sheets and rearranging a hard

00:12:43.519 --> 00:12:47.440
drive, for example. Your brain needs to

00:12:45.200 --> 00:12:48.480
know exactly what needs to be done and

00:12:47.440 --> 00:12:50.480
what that [music] looks like. Number

00:12:48.480 --> 00:12:52.160
four, wrong difficulty level. So, let's

